+Routing logic:
+1. The very first assistant turn (no history yet) is sent to the cheap model –
+   this already existed.
+2. We additionally detect the common tool-call pattern `tool → assistant → user`.
+   When the conversation ends with that sequence, the upcoming assistant turn
+   is almost always a *pure* JSON tool call.  Those mechanical calls can be
+   safely handled by the cheaper `gpt-4.1-mini` while all reasoning-heavy
+   turns (including the assistant response to the tool output) stay on the
+   stronger `gpt-4.1` model.
+
+Only the allowed model names are used.
 """
 
 from __future__ import annotations
+from typing import List, Dict, Any
+
+Message = Dict[str, Any]
 
 
